{"id":"4b7c0bd067b10e8c52d9bf623b7ba17b38b8819f","axis":"silent","repo":"elastic/elasticsearch","sha":"4b7c0bd067b10e8c52d9bf623b7ba17b38b8819f","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"docs/changelog/162962.yaml","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@","+area: Search","+issues:","+ - 162694","+pr: 162962","+summary: Fix knn filters on nested vectors that returned no hits or the wrong hits","+type: bug"],"additions":6,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/reference/query-languages/query-dsl/query-dsl-knn-query.md","lines":["@@ -253,13 +253,33 @@ The `knn` query can be used inside a nested query. The behaviour here is similar"," * kNN search over nested `dense_vector`s diversifies the top results over the top-level document"," * `filter` both over the top-level document metadata and `nested` is supported and acts as a pre-filter"," ","-To ensure correct results: each individual filter must be either over:","+:::::{applies-switch}","+","+::::{applies-item} stack: ga 9.6+","+Filters can use any query type and can mix top-level and `nested` fields. For example, a `bool` filter can combine fields from different levels in its `must`, `should`, and `must_not` clauses, and a `nested` filter can match a different nested object in the same document.","+","+{{es}} evaluates each filter at the nesting level of the fields it reads. A vector passes the filter when its own nested object matches, or when its enclosing object at that level matches.","+","+:::{note}","+The following filters keep the 9.5 and earlier behavior:","+","+- Filters that only read runtime fields, scripts, or fields copied with `include_in_parent` or `include_in_root`. {{es}} can't determine their nesting level.","+- `combined_fields` queries and `cross_fields` `multi_match` queries over fields from several levels. These aren't split by level.","+:::","+::::","+","+::::{applies-item} stack: ga 9.2-9.5","+Each filter must target only one of the following:"," "," - Top-level metadata","-- `nested` metadata {applies_to}`stack: ga 9.2`","-  :::{note}","-  A single knn query supports multiple filters, where some filters can be over the top-level metadata and some over nested.","-  :::","+- `nested` metadata","+","+:::{note}","+A single knn query supports multiple filters, where some filters can be over the top-level metadata and some over nested.","+:::","+::::","+","+:::::"," "," ### Basic nested knn search"," "],"additions":25,"deletions":5,"truncated":false},{"path":"rest-api-spec/src/yamlRestTest/resources/rest-api-spec/test/search.vectors/130_knn_query_nested_search.yml","lines":["@@ -585,14 +585,10 @@ setup:","   - match: { hits.hits.0._id: \"3\" }"," "," ---","-\"Test filter on sibling nested fields doesn't work\":","+\"Test filter on sibling nested fields\":","   - requires:","-      capabilities:","-        - method: POST","-          path: /_search","-          capabilities: [ knn_filter_on_nested_fields ]","-      test_runner_features: [\"capabilities\", \"close_to\"]","-      reason: \"Capability for filtering on nested fields required\"","+      cluster_features: \"search.vectors.knn_filter_nested_levels\"","+      reason: \"knn filters are evaluated at the nested level of the fields they read\""," ","   - do:","       search:","@@ -619,5 +615,41 @@ setup:","                                 nested2.value: \"domestic\"","               inner_hits: { size: 3, \"fields\": [ \"nested.paragraph_id\", \"nested.language\"], _source: false }"," ","-  - match: { hits.total.value: 0 }","+  - match: { hits.total.value: 2 }","+  - match: { hits.hits.0._id: \"3\" }","+  - length: { hits.hits.0.inner_hits.nested.hits.hits: 1 }","+  - match: { hits.hits.1._id: \"1\" }","+  - length: { hits.hits.1.inner_hits.nested.hits.hits: 2 }","+","+","+---","+\"Test non-term filter on the vector's nested fields\":","+  - requires:","+      cluster_features: \"search.vectors.knn_filter_nested_levels\"","+      reason: \"knn filters are evaluated at the nested level of the fields they read\""," ","+  - do:",